{"messages":[{"role":"system","content":"You are ThreadSense grounding verifier. You verify independently of the drafting agent; you judge and never repair.\nYour personal goal is: Judge every statement against the full topic context and decide whether the passed premises justify the exact proposed action."},{"role":"user","content":"\nCurrent Task: Judge each statement against the evidence it cites, read within the full context provided: every message of every member thread (with canonical author IDs, roles, thread starters and reactions) and every retrieved source for this topic. Citing a source is not support. A statement is SUPPORTED only if its cited evidence states or directly entails it and nothing in the context contradicts it; PARTIALLY_SUPPORTED if a material part is missing or the context qualifies it; UNSUPPORTED otherwise. A status line marking an excerpt historical, unresolved or a prior record means it cannot support what applies now. By kind: CLAIM_INCIDENT_FACT is a report of what members say, not a verified cause; CLAIM_SOURCE_FACT is SUPPORTED if the cited source says it, described with its status and dates; it establishes no current handling, procedure or destination; CLAIM_CAUSE needs verification in the cited evidence; a Verbatim quote must match its source, a Paraphrase must preserve the meaning. Prose names no one: role wording (\"the team lead instructs\", \"a tutor reports\") must match the cited author's role and act (reported, asked, confirmed or instructed), plural wording needs that many distinct cited authors, and listed attributions must hold (AUTHOR wrote the cited message, THREAD_STARTER started its thread, PARTICIPANT posted in it). A retrieved record's authorship is separate from its authority: an approver or recorder (actor_relation RECORD_AUTHORITY) is not its author, and a record whose authorship is not verified names no author. SUMMARY and SEVERITY_RATIONALE must follow from the evidence with no added cause, count or outcome. A SUMMARY sentence (statement_id summary:s1, summary:s2, ...) is judged on its own and shown only if SUPPORTED; its attributions name the people its role wording refers to, and wording that groups several people is SUPPORTED only if what it says they asked or reported is stated in each of their cited messages. A SUMMARY sentence with depends_on is read after the sentences it lists (for words such as \"this\" or \"their\"), but judged only on what it adds. A DETAIL sentence (statement_id detail:d1, detail:d2, ...) is shown when the card is opened and is judged exactly like a SUMMARY sentence: on its own, shown only if SUPPORTED, read after the sentences in its depends_on but judged only on what it adds. NO_ACTION_RATIONALE is the advisor's reason for proposing no further intervention now: SUPPORTED only if the cited evidence shows that reason and the context shows no unresolved handling question, guidance gap, applicable pending decision or operational problem that needs coordination; existing guidance does not by itself establish that no action is needed. ACTION and ALTERNATIVE are recommendations: judge whether their premises are supported, whether the action applies to this topic and whether the rationale follows; a source need not literally prescribe the action. Recipients and routes: keep apart what an action recommends, the functional recipient it proposes (engineering, a specialist, a QA reviewer) and any concrete route it names (a specific thread, channel, person or queue it goes to or through). A proposed functional recipient is justified by supported incident evidence showing a problem that needs that recipient's expertise; evidence of an established intake route is not required, and mentioning the recipient justifies nothing by itself. A concrete route, or a claim that a route is designated, official or mandatory, is a claim of its own and needs a premise whose evidence establishes it; an example-collection or status note asks people where to post examples and does not make that thread an intake route. The recommendation stays advisory (the team lead decides; it need not be shown to be the required or only next step): when no evidence names the concrete route, leave it unspecified (\"report it to engineering\") rather than choosing one. Judge a proposed recipient the same way in ACTION, ALTERNATIVE, INTERVENTION_NEED, ACTION_RATIONALE and REVIEW_NOTE: on whether the incident evidence shows a problem that needs that recipient's expertise, never on whether an intake route is on record; a statement that proposes a recipient and leaves the concrete route unspecified is not PARTIALLY_SUPPORTED, UNSUPPORTED or insufficient for that reason. ACTION and operational ALTERNATIVE statements list their premises: PENDING_YOUR_VERDICT premises are judged here and are provisional, not final; REJECTED ones failed deterministic checks and support nothing; a premise with depends_on stands only if every ANNOUNCEMENT_HANDLING statement it lists is also SUPPORTED. ACTION_CHOICE is SUPPORTED only if the cited evidence really leaves that choice between the named actions open (not merely an imagined alternative, a review flag or an unknown cause). INTERVENTION_NEED says why intervening now is needed: SUPPORTED only if the context shows that reason (an unresolved handling question, a guidance gap, an applicable pending decision, or an operational problem that needs coordination). Questions already answered in their threads are not unresolved; a general benefit (\"a reminder might help\") is not a need; existing guidance does not by itself rule a need out. Judge in this order: (1) announcement handling; (2) each premise's final status, which is your verdict on it combined with its dependencies; (3) sufficiency. Fill action_sufficiency for the ACTION and one alternative_sufficiency entry (with its statement_id) for each ALTERNATIVE that lists premises: SUFFICIENT only if premises whose final status is SUPPORTED justify the exact text as worded, including its conditions and scope; essential_statement_ids lists the premises it cannot stand without (each must have final status SUPPORTED); INSUFFICIENT if its exact text relies on a rejected, unsupported or dependency-voided premise or goes beyond its premises; a listed premise the text does not rely on is not essential, and its failure alone does not make the action insufficient. ACTION_RATIONALE is judged separately and may also cite context claims; action_sufficiency null if no ACTION statement is sent. SOURCE_AGREEMENT is SUPPORTED only if the named current sources say the same thing on the point in conflict and only the superseded material differs. A request by anyone but a team lead is a CLAIM_INCIDENT_FACT: SUPPORTED if that person asked it, and it carries no authority. CLAIM_THREAD_INSTRUCTION is a team lead's in-thread instruction: SUPPORTED only if that message gives it and it applies to the threads in scope; it is not project guidance. HISTORICAL_RECURRENCE needs retrieved records of earlier occurrences; REPORTED_RECURRENCE only needs members saying it is happening again. AFFECTED_REPORTER needs that person's own message reporting that they are affected. RESOLUTION is judged against the member's complete thread, including messages the statement did not cite. ANNOUNCEMENT_HANDLING needs the announcement to give that directive for this topic's project, batch and problem, and it governs only what it directs (a request to post examples governs where examples go, not escalation or an intake route); a routine reminder or schedule directs nothing for the topic. OPEN_QUESTION is SUPPORTED only if the guidance and decisions in the context really leave that specific question unsettled and it is a handling or policy question for the team lead; a not-yet-diagnosed cause, pending diagnostic results or a pending expert assessment is not one. Return exactly one verdict for every statement_id. The team lead reads SUMMARY, DETAIL, ACTION (label, instruction, draft to copy, scope and changes), ACTION_RATIONALE, NO_ACTION_RATIONALE, REVIEW_NOTE and OPEN_QUESTION exactly as written: judge that exact text, including its conditions, uncertainty, scope and who reported, asked, confirmed or instructed; plain wording is expected, but it must not overstate the evidence. A quoted passage must match its source exactly. open_review_flags lists the upstream review obligations still open on these threads; a REVIEW_NOTE may rely on them. Source consistency (always fill source_consistency, even when the draft declares no conflict): compare the governing_sources that address the handling question of this topic with each other, independently of the draft. List sources that state the same rule as AGREE, and sources that state different rules for the same cases as CONFLICT with the point and disagreement_scope (which cases, batch or section differ). assessed_evidence_ids lists the governing sources you compared; relations may be empty when they address different points. Only governing sources count: historical, superseded, expired or withdrawn material, prior records and member messages are not current sources, an announcement governs only if it directs handling for this topic, and members disagreeing with each other is not a source conflict. For each entry in declared_conflicts give one declared_conflict_checks entry: CONFIRMED (the cited sources state different rules on that point), SOURCES_AGREE (they say the same thing; only wording or detail differs) or UNDETERMINED.\n\nInput JSON:\n{\"topic\": {\"project_id\": \"multilingual_eval\", \"batch_id\": \"multi_batch_11\", \"candidate_group_id\": \"cluster_398a1390e27da753\", \"topic_id\": \"cluster_398a1390e27da753/topic_1\", \"topic_label\": \"LT Hangul rendering issue\", \"projection_gap\": null, \"as_of\": \"2026-10-02T12:00:00Z\", \"member_ids\": [\"member_de85059f17dd8949093893e5\", \"member_ba4581cf60461d619dc34676\"]}, \"statements\": [{\"statement_id\": \"claim:c1\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_INCIDENT_FACT\", \"text\": \"A QA tutor reports that Hangul appears as boxes in LT. Verbatim quote: \\\"Hangul appears as boxes in LT.\\\"\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_MULTI_QA:1790885224.000166\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U008\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_MULTI_QA:1790885224.000166\", \"role\": \"QA_TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c2\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_INCIDENT_FACT\", \"text\": \"A tutor reports Hangul rendering as boxes on the LT rating screen for MULTI-7548 and asks whether others see it.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_MULTI_GENERAL:1790927548.000165\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U017\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_MULTI_GENERAL:1790927548.000165\", \"role\": \"TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c3\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_INCIDENT_FACT\", \"text\": \"A tutor reports Korean glyphs vanishing in the preview while Latin text is visible. Verbatim quote: \\\"Korean glyphs vanish in the preview while Latin text is visible.\\\"\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_MULTI_GENERAL:1790927595.000113\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U013\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_MULTI_GENERAL:1790927595.000113\", \"role\": \"TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c4\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_INCIDENT_FACT\", \"text\": \"A QA tutor asks in the MULTI-7548 thread whether the original text displays correctly outside the labeling tool. Verbatim quote: \\\"Does the original text display correctly outside the labeling tool?\\\"\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_MULTI_GENERAL:1790927640.000226\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U019\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_MULTI_GENERAL:1790927640.000226\", \"role\": \"QA_TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c5\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_THREAD_INSTRUCTION\", \"text\": \"The team lead instructs the MULTI-7548 thread to treat the item as a tool-rendering incident rather than a language-quality mistake if the original text renders outside LT but not inside it. Verbatim quote: \\\"If the original text renders outside LT but not inside it, treat this item as a tool-rendering incident, not a language-quality mistake.\\\"\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_MULTI_GENERAL:1790927684.000339\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U001\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_MULTI_GENERAL:1790927684.000339\", \"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c6\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_GUIDANCE\", \"text\": \"The current FAQ directs reporting a tool-rendering incident when characters appear as boxes or become unreadable in LT, checking the text outside LT where possible, and not claiming the underlying response has corrupted characters before that comparison is available.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"k:multilingual-eval-faq@1.1:e2ea02bf\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c7\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_GUIDANCE\", \"text\": \"The current instructions treat boxes or broken characters in LT as tool-rendering incidents until the source text is checked, require capturing task IDs, and direct recording any inability to compare outside LT rather than asserting corrupt model text; operational impact is assessed separately from language-quality grades.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"k:multilingual-eval-instructions@1.2:ea925467\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c8\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_INFERENCE\", \"text\": \"The provided MULTI-7548 thread messages do not contain an outside-LT comparison result.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_MULTI_GENERAL:1790927548.000165\", \"m:C_MULTI_GENERAL:1790927595.000113\", \"m:C_MULTI_GENERAL:1790927640.000226\", \"m:C_MULTI_GENERAL:1790927684.000339\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"summary:s1\", \"kind\": \"SUMMARY\", \"text\": \"A QA tutor and two tutors report Hangul displaying as boxes or disappearing in LT.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_MULTI_QA:1790885224.000166\", \"m:C_MULTI_GENERAL:1790927548.000165\", \"m:C_MULTI_GENERAL:1790927595.000113\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U008\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_MULTI_QA:1790885224.000166\", \"role\": \"QA_TUTOR\"}, {\"user_id\": \"U017\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_MULTI_GENERAL:1790927548.000165\", \"role\": \"TUTOR\"}, {\"user_id\": \"U013\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_MULTI_GENERAL:1790927595.000113\", \"role\": \"TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"summary:s2\", \"kind\": \"SUMMARY\", \"text\": \"Current guidance calls for reporting a tool-rendering incident and checking the text outside LT where possible, rather than assuming the underlying response contains corrupted characters.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"k:multilingual-eval-faq@1.1:e2ea02bf\", \"k:multilingual-eval-instructions@1.2:ea925467\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"detail:d1\", \"kind\": \"DETAIL\", \"text\": \"A QA tutor reports boxes in LT; a tutor reports boxes on the rating screen for MULTI-7548.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_MULTI_QA:1790885224.000166\", \"m:C_MULTI_GENERAL:1790927548.000165\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U008\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_MULTI_QA:1790885224.000166\", \"role\": \"QA_TUTOR\"}, {\"user_id\": \"U017\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_MULTI_GENERAL:1790927548.000165\", \"role\": \"TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"detail:d2\", \"kind\": \"DETAIL\", \"text\": \"A second tutor reports Korean glyphs disappearing in the preview while Latin text remains visible.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_MULTI_GENERAL:1790927595.000113\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U013\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_MULTI_GENERAL:1790927595.000113\", \"role\": \"TUTOR\"}], \"depends_on\": [\"detail:d1\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"detail:d3\", \"kind\": \"DETAIL\", \"text\": \"In the MULTI-7548 thread, a QA tutor asks whether the original text displays correctly outside LT; no comparison result appears in the provided messages.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_MULTI_GENERAL:1790927640.000226\", \"m:C_MULTI_GENERAL:1790927548.000165\", \"m:C_MULTI_GENERAL:1790927595.000113\", \"m:C_MULTI_GENERAL:1790927684.000339\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U019\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_MULTI_GENERAL:1790927640.000226\", \"role\": \"QA_TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"detail:d4\", \"kind\": \"DETAIL\", \"text\": \"The team lead instructs that thread to treat the item as a tool-rendering incident, not a language-quality mistake, if the original text renders outside LT but not inside it.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_MULTI_GENERAL:1790927684.000339\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U001\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_MULTI_GENERAL:1790927684.000339\", \"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\"}], \"depends_on\": [\"detail:d3\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"action\", \"kind\": \"ACTION\", \"text\": \"Report a technical issue to engineering. Instruction: Report the Hangul display failures to engineering, grouping the reported symptoms and including MULTI-7548 as the available task reference. Draft to copy: Engineering: please investigate these Hangul display reports in LT.\\n- A QA tutor and a tutor report Hangul appearing as boxes; the tutor identifies MULTI-7548 on the rating screen.\\n- A second tutor reports Korean glyphs disappearing in the preview while Latin text remains visible.\\nAffected reporters: please provide task IDs and compare the original text outside LT where possible. If comparison is unavailable, record that limitation. Treat these as tool-rendering incidents pending source-text checks, separately from language-quality grades; do not assume the underlying response contains corrupted characters. Scope: Report the observed display symptoms without asserting a technical cause or treating the thread-specific instruction as project-wide guidance.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_MULTI_QA:1790885224.000166\", \"m:C_MULTI_GENERAL:1790927548.000165\", \"m:C_MULTI_GENERAL:1790927595.000113\", \"k:multilingual-eval-faq@1.1:e2ea02bf\", \"k:multilingual-eval-instructions@1.2:ea925467\"], \"premises\": [{\"statement_id\": \"claim:c1\", \"status\": \"PENDING_YOUR_VERDICT\"}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c2\", \"status\": \"PENDING_YOUR_VERDICT\"}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c3\", \"status\": \"PENDING_YOUR_VERDICT\"}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c6\", \"status\": \"PENDING_YOUR_VERDICT\"}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c7\", \"status\": \"PENDING_YOUR_VERDICT\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"action:rationale\", \"kind\": \"ACTION_RATIONALE\", \"text\": \"Why this helps: Comparable display failures across three reporters warrant engineering investigation. Current guidance directs incident reporting without waiting for a confirmed cause or completed source-text comparison.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_MULTI_QA:1790885224.000166\", \"m:C_MULTI_GENERAL:1790927548.000165\", \"m:C_MULTI_GENERAL:1790927595.000113\", \"k:multilingual-eval-faq@1.1:e2ea02bf\", \"k:multilingual-eval-instructions@1.2:ea925467\", \"m:C_MULTI_GENERAL:1790927640.000226\", \"m:C_MULTI_GENERAL:1790927684.000339\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"action:need\", \"kind\": \"INTERVENTION_NEED\", \"text\": \"Why intervening now is needed (an operational problem that needs coordination): A QA tutor and two tutors report comparable Hangul display failures in LT, warranting technical investigation while source-text checks are collected.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_MULTI_QA:1790885224.000166\", \"m:C_MULTI_GENERAL:1790927548.000165\", \"m:C_MULTI_GENERAL:1790927595.000113\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"resolution:member_de85059f17dd8949093893e5\", \"kind\": \"RESOLUTION\", \"text\": \"Member thread member_de85059f17dd8949093893e5 is UNRESOLVED: The QA tutor's thread contains a report of Hangul boxes but no response, comparison result or resolution.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_MULTI_QA:1790885224.000166\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"resolution:member_ba4581cf60461d619dc34676\", \"kind\": \"RESOLUTION\", \"text\": \"Member thread member_ba4581cf60461d619dc34676 is PARTIALLY_RESOLVED: The team lead gives conditional handling for the tutor's item, but the thread contains neither the requested outside-LT comparison result nor confirmation that the display problem is resolved.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_MULTI_GENERAL:1790927548.000165\", \"m:C_MULTI_GENERAL:1790927595.000113\", \"m:C_MULTI_GENERAL:1790927640.000226\", \"m:C_MULTI_GENERAL:1790927684.000339\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"severity:rationale\", \"kind\": \"SEVERITY_RATIONALE\", \"text\": \"Severity HIGH: A QA tutor and two tutors report comparable Korean-text display failures within the same batch and time window, suggesting broader disruption to evaluating that text.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_MULTI_QA:1790885224.000166\", \"m:C_MULTI_GENERAL:1790927548.000165\", \"m:C_MULTI_GENERAL:1790927595.000113\", \"m:C_MULTI_GENERAL:1790927640.000226\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"severity:signal:HIGH[3]\", \"kind\": \"SEVERITY_SIGNAL\", \"text\": \"Rubric signal met - \\\"Multiple distinct people or affected tasks reporting a comparable problem within the relevant project, batch, and time window, suggesting broader disruption or systemic labeling risk. Consider the number affected relative to the known active group when that information is available; do not require an explicit statement of widespread impact\\\": A QA tutor reports Hangul boxes in LT; a tutor reports boxes on the rating screen; a second tutor reports Korean glyphs disappearing in the preview while Latin text remains visible.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_MULTI_QA:1790885224.000166\", \"m:C_MULTI_GENERAL:1790927548.000165\", \"m:C_MULTI_GENERAL:1790927595.000113\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"reporter:U008\", \"kind\": \"AFFECTED_REPORTER\", \"text\": \"U008 reports, in their own cited message, being affected by this problem.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_MULTI_QA:1790885224.000166\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"reporter:U017\", \"kind\": \"AFFECTED_REPORTER\", \"text\": \"U017 reports, in their own cited message, being affected by this problem.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_MULTI_GENERAL:1790927548.000165\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"reporter:U013\", \"kind\": \"AFFECTED_REPORTER\", \"text\": \"U013 reports, in their own cited message, being affected by this problem.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_MULTI_GENERAL:1790927595.000113\"]}], \"member_threads\": [{\"evidence_id\": \"m:C_MULTI_QA:1790885224.000166\", \"origin\": \"member_message\", \"use\": \"MEMBER_REPORT\", \"member_id\": \"member_de85059f17dd8949093893e5\", \"thread_id\": \"1790885224.000166\", \"author_id\": \"U008\", \"author_role\": \"QA_TUTOR\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-01T20:07:04.000166Z\", \"thread_starter_id\": \"U008\", \"thread_starter_role\": \"QA_TUTOR\", \"excerpt\": \"Hangul appears as boxes in LT.\", \"instruction_authority\": \"NONE\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"m:C_MULTI_GENERAL:1790927548.000165\", \"origin\": \"member_message\", \"use\": \"MEMBER_REPORT\", \"member_id\": \"member_ba4581cf60461d619dc34676\", \"thread_id\": \"1790927548.000165\", \"author_id\": \"U017\", \"author_role\": \"TUTOR\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-02T07:52:28.000165Z\", \"thread_starter_id\": \"U017\", \"thread_starter_role\": \"TUTOR\", \"excerpt\": \"Anyone else seeing this? Hangul in LT renders as □□□ on the rating screen. (task ref MULTI-7548)\", \"instruction_authority\": \"NONE\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"m:C_MULTI_GENERAL:1790927595.000113\", \"origin\": \"member_message\", \"use\": \"MEMBER_REPORT\", \"member_id\": \"member_ba4581cf60461d619dc34676\", \"thread_id\": \"1790927548.000165\", \"author_id\": \"U013\", \"author_role\": \"TUTOR\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-02T07:53:15.000113Z\", \"thread_starter_id\": \"U017\", \"thread_starter_role\": \"TUTOR\", \"excerpt\": \"Korean glyphs vanish in the preview while Latin text is visible.\", \"instruction_authority\": \"NONE\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"m:C_MULTI_GENERAL:1790927640.000226\", \"origin\": \"member_message\", \"use\": \"MEMBER_REPORT\", \"member_id\": \"member_ba4581cf60461d619dc34676\", \"thread_id\": \"1790927548.000165\", \"author_id\": \"U019\", \"author_role\": \"QA_TUTOR\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-02T07:54:00.000226Z\", \"thread_starter_id\": \"U017\", \"thread_starter_role\": \"TUTOR\", \"excerpt\": \"Does the original text display correctly outside the labeling tool?\", \"instruction_authority\": \"NONE\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"m:C_MULTI_GENERAL:1790927684.000339\", \"origin\": \"member_message\", \"use\": \"MEMBER_REPORT\", \"member_id\": \"member_ba4581cf60461d619dc34676\", \"thread_id\": \"1790927548.000165\", \"author_id\": \"U001\", \"author_role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-02T07:54:44.000339Z\", \"thread_starter_id\": \"U017\", \"thread_starter_role\": \"TUTOR\", \"excerpt\": \"If the original text renders outside LT but not inside it, treat this item as a tool-rendering incident, not a language-quality mistake.\", \"instruction_authority\": \"THREAD_SCOPE\"}], \"retrieved_sources\": [{\"evidence_id\": \"k:multilingual-eval-faq@1.1:e2ea02bf\", \"origin\": \"retrieved_source\", \"use\": \"CURRENT_GUIDANCE\", \"citation\": {\"authoring\": \"multilingual-eval-faq@1.1\", \"title\": \"Multilingual Evaluation — FAQ (v1.1)\", \"sections\": [\"Tool issues\"], \"source\": {\"manual_key\": \"multilingual-eval-faq\", \"system\": \"manual\"}}, \"source_type\": \"faq\", \"record_kind\": \"faq\", \"applicability\": {\"state\": \"CURRENT\", \"revision_state\": \"CURRENT\", \"version_mode\": \"current\"}, \"dates\": {\"source_date\": \"2026-09-18T13:00:00Z\", \"basis\": \"effective_at\", \"effective_at\": \"2026-09-18T13:00:00Z\", \"expired_as_of\": false}, \"scope\": {\"project_id\": \"multilingual_eval\", \"scope\": \"project\", \"batch_relation\": \"project_wide\"}, \"authority\": {\"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\", \"actor\": \"U001\", \"actor_relation\": \"RECORD_AUTHORITY\", \"approval_status\": \"EXPLICIT_SOURCE_MARKER\", \"provenance\": \"synthetic_manual_record\"}, \"authorship\": {\"verified\": false, \"basis\": \"NO_AUTHOR_RECORDED\"}, \"recorded_states\": {\"status\": \"approved\"}, \"excerpt\": \"## Tool issues\\n\\n### Q: Characters or tone marks appear as boxes or become unreadable in LT.\\nReport a tool-rendering incident and check the text outside LT where possible. Until that comparison is available, do not claim the underlying response itself has corrupted characters.\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"k:multilingual-eval-faq@1.1:8508b653\", \"origin\": \"retrieved_source\", \"use\": \"CURRENT_GUIDANCE\", \"citation\": {\"authoring\": \"multilingual-eval-faq@1.1\", \"title\": \"Multilingual Evaluation — FAQ (v1.1)\", \"sections\": [\"Language adherence\"], \"source\": {\"manual_key\": \"multilingual-eval-faq\", \"system\": \"manual\"}}, \"source_type\": \"faq\", \"record_kind\": \"faq\", \"applicability\": {\"state\": \"CURRENT\", \"revision_state\": \"CURRENT\", \"version_mode\": \"current\"}, \"dates\": {\"source_date\": \"2026-09-18T13:00:00Z\", \"basis\": \"effective_at\", \"effective_at\": \"2026-09-18T13:00:00Z\", \"expired_as_of\": false}, \"scope\": {\"project_id\": \"multilingual_eval\", \"scope\": \"project\", \"batch_relation\": \"project_wide\"}, \"authority\": {\"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\", \"actor\": \"U001\", \"actor_relation\": \"RECORD_AUTHORITY\", \"approval_status\": \"EXPLICIT_SOURCE_MARKER\", \"provenance\": \"synthetic_manual_record\"}, \"authorship\": {\"verified\": false, \"basis\": \"NO_AUTHOR_RECORDED\"}, \"recorded_states\": {\"status\": \"approved\"}, \"excerpt\": \"## Language adherence\\n\\n### Q: Does a single English word in a Korean or Japanese answer count as code-switching?\\nNot automatically. Ordinary loanwords are acceptable. Assess the word in context and against the required output language; an unrequested full paragraph in another language is a different issue.\\n\\n### Q: The user code-switched. Should the response mirror it?\\nCheck the explicit output-language requirement and context. User code-switching alone does not settle the score.\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"k:multilingual-eval-instructions@1.2:ea925467\", \"origin\": \"retrieved_source\", \